      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Titanium-sapphire technology and passive mode locking transformed ultrafast science and made attosecond physics possible.",
        "attribution": "Moulton's laser medium, Keller's mode-locking advances, and Sibbett's pioneering ultrafast work form a coherent account.",
        "maturity": "The impact has endured for decades across fundamental spectroscopy and precision control.",
        "uncertainties": ["The technical and conceptual lineage includes many contributors, so a three-person attribution requires careful historical delimitation."]
      }
    },
